From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:36:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mf, winegstreamer: V4L2 video capture sources (3299)

Video capture: MFEnumDeviceSources(VIDCAP) lists the V4L2 cameras
(scanned in /dev/video*, only nodes that capture video), and
MFCreateDeviceSource / MFCreateDeviceSourceActivate / IMFActivate give an
IMFMediaSourceEx (live, one stream) for a camera. winegstreamer gets a new
unix part (wg_capture.c): a GStreamer pipeline v4l2src ! capsfilter !
[jpegdec] ! videoconvert ! capsfilter into a private sink pad, a frame
queue of four (the oldest frame goes when the consumer is slow), and
timestamps from the pipeline. The native types are YUY2 and NV12 for each
mode the camera has (a JPEG-only mode is decoded). Samples go out only
for outstanding RequestSample calls; Start applies the type chosen on the
presentation descriptor, restarting the device for a new type.

Test hook: WINE_SG_FAKE_CAMERAS=raw,jpeg (or none) replaces the device
scan with fake cameras made from a live videotestsrc and never touches a
/dev/video node. Test: test/fastvidcap-gate.sh (probe run 64- and 32-bit;
mutants SG_MUTANT_VC_*).

